config VIDEO_HISTB_VDEC
	tristate "HiSilicon HiSTB video decoder driver"
	depends on ARCH_HISI || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on V4L_MEM2MEM_DRIVERS
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
	select V4L2_MEM2MEM_DEV
	select V4L2_H264
	help
	  Support for the VDH hardware video decoder on HiSilicon Hi3798MV100
	  and Hi3716CV200 set-top-box SoCs. The driver implements the V4L2
	  stateless decoder interface: the bitstream is parsed in userspace and
	  submitted through request controls, and the hardware decodes H.264,
	  HEVC, MPEG-2, MPEG-4 and H.263 into 16x16-tiled NV21 frames. The
	  Hi3716CV200's generation of the block has no HEVC path, so that
	  profile is only negotiable on Hi3798MV100.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called histb-vdec.
